      "content": "99|| Rumor gathering | Drinks, tips, or favors | Better rumors cost more than coin |\n100|\n101|---\n102|\n103|## Faction Presence\n104|\n105|The guildhall is neutral ground in theory and a negotiation pit in practice. Representatives, recruiters, and spies from many groups pass through looking for talent.\n106|\n107|Possible visitors include:\n108|\n109|- [[Ashen Shadow Society]] bounty handlers looking for discreet monster work\n110|- [[Tribunal Highblade Coalition]] officers seeking lawful mercenaries\n111|- [[The Loot Tavern]] contacts interested in monster components and field reports\n112|- Local nobles posting public contracts through [[The Rolling Papers]]\n113|- Underworld fixers passing jobs through [[The Roach Clip]]\n114|- Scholars from [[N.E.R.D]] seeking field researchers and magical samples\n115|- Growers, alchemists, and merchants interested in [[Arcannabis]]-related problems\n116|\n117|---\n118|\n119|## Rules of the Hall\n120|\n121|1. Do not start fights inside the guildhall.\n122|2. Do not steal from the job board.\n123|3. Do not bring in live monsters without warning the clerk.\n124|4. Do not leave cursed items unattended.\n125|5. If a posting says “do not alert the authorities,” do not read it out loud near authorities.\n126|6. Parties are temporary. Reputations are not.\n127|\n128|---\n129|\n130|## Rumors\n131|\n132|| d6 | Rumor |\n133||---:|---|\n134|| 1 | A public monster contract in [[The Rolling Papers]] was quietly edited after someone important complained. |\n135|| 2 | A Roach Clip job appeared on the back rail without anyone seeing who posted it. |",
