      "nextStartLine": 36,
      "content": "1|\n2|> *“No permanent party, no permanent problem.”*\n3|\n4|[![TC_The Adventurers Guildhall Night Characters_Interior Scene.jpg](https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/62750da488ff573e9bdc63c4/097ccf1b-7b44-4efd-8718-28b4da94edae/TC_The+Adventurers+Guildhall+Night+Characters_Interior+Scene.jpg)](https://www.tomcartos.com/adventurers-guildhall?itemId=tngvf4gvej5buyqrb5arpgscoykqsx)\n5|\n6|The **FLS Guildhall** is the informal headquarters of the [[Free League of Stickyickistan]], a loud, practical, semi-organized adventuring hub where rotating crews gather between jobs. It is less a noble institution and more a shared clubhouse, contract office, message board, tavern backroom, records archive, and monster-hunter break room all crammed under one roof.\n7|\n8|The guildhall serves the open-table nature of the Free League: adventurers come and go, parties form around posted jobs, DMs introduce new threats, and the setting grows through whatever survives contact with the players.\n9|\n10|## Overview\n11|\n12|**Type:** Adventurers’ guildhall / contract office / public tavern-adjacent headquarters  \n13|**Location:** [[Stickyickistan]]  \n14|**Affiliation:** [[Free League of Stickyickistan]]  \n15|**Known For:** Rotating parties, public contracts, monster hunts, shared rumors, and questionable paperwork  \n16|**Primary Notice Boards:** [[The Rolling Papers]] and [[The Roach Clip]]  \n17|\n18|---\n19|\n20|## Description\n21|\n22|The FLS Guildhall is always busy, but rarely organized. The front room smells like rain-soaked cloaks, old paper, smoke, cheap coffee, spilled malt, floor wax, and whatever monster part someone swore was “fully preserved.” Adventurers crowd the tables between jobs, comparing scars, arguing over maps, sharpening blades, filling out forms badly, and pretending not to listen when someone else mentions a better-paying contract.\n23|\n24|Maps of [[Mythmos]], [[Stickyickistan]], and distant trouble spots cover the walls, many of them pinned with colored string, bounty slips, wax seals, and handwritten corrections from adventurers who survived the trip. Public contracts, civic emergencies, missing-person notices, and monster attacks circulate openly through weekly copies of [[The Rolling Papers]]. Less official opportunities drift through the room in copies of [[The Roach Clip]], whispered referrals, folded notes, and conversations that become quieter when clerks walk past.\n25|\n26|The guildhall does not make the Free League tidy. It makes the chaos legible. The hall exists so dangerous people can find dangerous work in a place with witnesses, paperwork, rumors, and at least a thin chance of accountability before the next disaster gets worse.\n27|\n28|---\n29|\n30|## What Adventurers Can Do Here\n31|\n32|- Find public adventure postings from [[The Rolling Papers]]\n33|- Hear about discreet or illegal jobs from [[The Roach Clip]]\n34|- Form a party for a one-shot or short arc\n35|- Meet DMs, patrons, handlers, and faction contacts",
